  {
    "date": "2023-12-08",
    "term": "白い",
    "kana": "しろい",
    "meaning": "white",
    "level": "N5",
    "pos": ["adjective (keiyoushi)"],
    "priority": ["ichi1", "news1", "nf16"],
    "stratum": "wago",
    "processes": ["sound-change"],
    "headline": "Shiroi was shiroshi, and its medial k went through voicing, spirantization and gliding until it disappeared.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "Modern form of Old Japanese adjective しろし (shiroshi)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "⟨siro₁si⟩ (classical 終止形 (shūshikei) or terminal form) → ⟨siro₁ki₁⟩ (classical 連体形 (rentaikei) or attributive form) → /siroi/ (modern shūshikei and rentaikei)"
      },
      {
        "quote": "An intervocalic sound-change caused the medial plosive /-k-/ to undergo voicing, then spirantization, then gliding, then being dropped, before /-i, -u, -e, -o/ (Hamano, 2000)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "⟨siro₁ki₁⟩ → */sirʷokʲi/ → */sirʷogʲi/ → */sirʷoɣi/ → */sirʷoji/ → /siroi/ → [ɕiɾo̞i]."
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "id": 121438,
        "ja": "白いですか。",
        "en": "Is it white?",
        "enId": 282567,
        "form": "白い",
        "furigana": [["白", "しろ"], ["いですか。"]]
      },
      {
